Obviously a room designed to please the senses, Casimir apparrently spares no
effort in creating the most luxurious of living spaces.  Silken tapestries 
adorn every wall from floor to ceiling, spreading across the ground like 
cascading water where they meet the floor.  The thick, well-cushioned carpet
reminds you of a spring meadow after a light shower, cool and comforting. The 
Lord's bed is a sight in itself, and dominates the room.  It is built low to 
floor, to accomodate a child, but is excesssively wide, and is draped with silk
fabric on top of numerous featherbeds.  Cushions and a single opulent velvet 
blanket are pushed aside giving the bed a soft, inviting appearance.  Two 
candelabras on either side of the bed cast deep, flickering shadows over the
entire scene, adding to the ambience of the room.


